{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019xe79aXFL5jwWcojPwqnp8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Intervals.icu API workout_doc hr target units start end \"%lthr\" \"value\"\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"pkg.go.dev\",\"url\":\"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tomdiekmann/icu\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Upload planned workouts to Garmin Connect\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/upload-planned-workouts-to-garmin-connect/1521/157\"},{\"title\":\"Incorrect structured workout rendering in calendar export\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/incorrect-structured-workout-rendering-in-calendar-export/127096\"},{\"title\":\"Workout builder\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder/1163/839\"}]\n\nThe search turned up forum threads and one Go client, but nothing that documents the exact `%lthr` unit string in `workout_doc`. The closest evidence is indirect.\n\n- **Power units:** Example JSON exports show power steps as a \"power\" object holding a \"value\" and \"units\" field set to \"%ftp\". A later export uses a different form, a \"units\" of \"power_zone\" plus a \"_power\" object with start and end values.\n- **HR targets:** A user reported that HR-based workout editing could only support %HR, not absolute HR. The developer then added lthr, max_hr, threshold_pace and pace_units to the export.\n- **Range fields:** A developer explained that Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range, and for power this is only done for outdoor workouts. For HR it is 1.5%. The `_power` start and end fields appear even when a step has no explicit range, as one user noticed.\n- **Sending HR as LTHR:** A Garmin-sync thread says the target HR is sent as a percentage of LTHR, so mismatched LTHR values between apps cause incorrect zones.\n- **Third-party limits:** A TrainingPeaks-related user said that platform accepts only percentages of FTP, LTHR, and similar values, not raw watts or bpm.\n\nThe Go client shows a text form of targets, such as \"15 min at 55–75% FTP\", which suggests the text-based `workout_doc` uses percentage syntax. Verify the exact `%lthr` unit string against the official Intervals.icu API docs or a live download before relying on it.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2bea3dd-9e3e-4f96-bf4b-b795559c0a32","uuid":"dd859ffb-0ba6-44a0-8344-3c5708451079","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:25:06.228Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Intervals.icu API workout_doc hr target units start end \"%lthr\" \"value\"","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01D74cHHFZkSV7j1xi3FRhCm","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20"},{"title":"pkg.go.dev","url":"https://pkg.go.dev/github.com/tomdiekmann/icu"},{"title":"Feature request: Nativ