{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bgk9zDrvnT6zVSPDxBvq8A","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"intervals.icu workout_doc step \"hr\" \"units\" \"%lthr\" \"start\" \"end\" json example\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7\"},{\"title\":\"field descriptions\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/utils/field-descriptions.ts\"},{\"title\":\"API access to Intervals.icu\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax\",\"url\":\"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md\"},{\"title\":\"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356\"},{\"title\":\"Workout Builder: Duration types\",\"url\":\"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder-duration-types/69924\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a JSON example that uses HR with %LTHR units, so I can't confirm that exact format. The closest material is an Intervals.icu forum thread about the API, which shows the general pattern.\n\n- **Power example:** The forum thread shows a `workout_doc` with a top-level FTP value and steps that use `units` set to a power zone, plus a `_power` object holding resolved `start` and `end` values. That's the pattern a developer would mirror for HR. For power the athlete's FTP is included in the workout_doc field.\n- **Resolved ranges:** Fixed targets come back as a range with a `start` and `end`. Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range. For HR it is 1.5%. The `powerRange`, `hrRange` and `paceRange` query parameters can change that, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **HR-specific history:** A developer reported that HR based workouts editing can only support %HR (and not absolute HR), and asked for LTHR and max HR to be included. The developer later said I have added lthr, max_hr, threshold_pace and pace_units. The thread doesn't show whether this is in the output as a per-step `%lthr` unit.\n- **Syntax caveat:** Only a third-party Intervals.icu cycling syntax guide appeared in the results, and it covers percent of FTP and watts, not HR. Its examples don't show HR units.\n\nTo confirm the exact `hr` / `%lthr` step shape, download an HR-based workout from Intervals.icu (the thread's suggested approach) or check the official API docs. Note that the forum posts are from several years of API changes, so field names may have changed since.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2bea3dd-9e3e-4f96-bf4b-b795559c0a32","uuid":"375d73e6-e788-4538-a733-8e8b80b43033","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:25:15.069Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"intervals.icu workout_doc step \"hr\" \"units\" \"%lthr\" \"start\" \"end\" json example","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VVpWVAHFZw2naDYNyRAbUn","content":[{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=20"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/129"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609?page=7"},{"title":"field descriptions","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/utils/field-descriptions.ts"},{"title":"API access to Intervals.icu","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/api-access-to-intervals-icu/609/389"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Running Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/213d5f7b06df7793bfdba7feb49869bae4075379/src/resources/run-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"# Intervals.icu Cycling Workout Syntax","url":"https://glama.ai/mcp/servers/@gesteves/domestique/blob/20812aa55701874b27ac02c5fde692861f748452/src/resources/cycling-workout-syntax.md"},{"title":"Feature request: Native Heart Rate Reserve (%HRR / Karvonen) heart-rate zones","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/feature-request-native-heart-rate-reserve-hrr-karvonen-heart-rate-zones/132356"},{"title":"Workout Builder: Duration types","url":"https://forum.intervals.icu/t/workout-builder-duration-types/69924"}]},"The search didn't turn up a JSON example that uses HR with %LTHR units, so I can't confirm that exact format. The closest material is an Intervals.icu forum thread about the API, which shows the general pattern.\n\n- **Power example:** The forum thread shows a `workout_doc` with a top-level FTP value and steps that use `units` set to a power zone, plus a `_power` object holding resolved `start` and `end` values. That's the pattern a developer would mirror for HR. For power the athlete's FTP is included in the workout_doc field.\n- **Resolved ranges:** Fixed targets come back as a range with a `start` and `end`. Intervals.icu translates fixed power (and other) targets into a range. For HR it is 1.5%. The `powerRange`, `hrRange` and `paceRange` query parameters can change that, and use 0.0 to disable range.\n- **HR-specific history:** A developer reported that HR based workouts editing can only support %HR (and not absolute HR), and asked for LTHR and max HR to be included. The developer later said I have added lthr, max_hr, threshold_pace and pace_units. The thread doesn't show whether this is in the output as a per-step `%lthr` unit.\n- **Syntax caveat:** Only a third-party Intervals.icu cycling syntax guide appeared in the results, and it covers percent of FTP and watts, not HR. Its examples don't show HR units.\n\nTo confirm the exact `hr` / `%lthr` step shape, download an HR-based workout from Intervals.icu (the thread's suggested approach) or check the official API docs. Note that the forum posts are from several years of API changes, so field names may have changed since."],"durationSeconds":7.121885333999999,"searchCount":1},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Bgk9zDrvnT6zVSPDxBvq8A","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
