{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAoYP5twC2y5rnsLajqG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ANP8KrcftzjhZBk1kQ5ovg","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-wAUkn2/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` sent every HR corridor as a percentage of LTHR:\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 88, \"end\": 93}\n```\n\nIntervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`), but\nwhen the workout reached the Forerunner 965 the target was resolved against the\nwatch's own zone bands, so each planned corridor displayed as a zone edge. The\nwatch's LTHR (168) differs from the athlete's (172), which is why the bands\nmoved but still never matched the planned range.\n\n## Change\n\n- **`gen.py`**: `hr_target()` now resolves the planned percentage to absolute\n  bpm using the plan's LTHR, and emits `\"units\": \"bpm\"`:\n  `value = round(lthr * lo / 100)`, `end = round(lthr * hi / 100)`.\n  `build_doc()` passes `plan[\"lthr\"]` down to each step. A plan without `lthr`\n  now fails with `KeyError` rather than silently using a default.\n- **`plans/tempo-run.json`**: added `\"lthr\": 172`.\n- **`README.md`**: corrected the note that said Intervals converts %LTHR to bpm\n  at export. The conversion now happens in `gen.py`.\n\n## Check\n\nRegenerated the event locally (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json`, not\npushed). The targets match the \"expected on watch\" column in\n`readback/watch-notes.md`:\n\n| step | planned | new target (bpm) | watch-notes expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 % | 117–129 | 117–129 |\n| Tempo | 88–93 % | 151–160 | 151–160 |\n| Float | 75–82 % | 129–141 | 129–141 |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 % | 112–124 | 112–124 |\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not push and have no live API or watch access here, so I have **not**\n  confirmed that Intervals exports `\"units\": \"bpm\"` targets to Garmin as custom\n  ranges. The watch-notes say an earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt displayed\n  214–249 bpm. The payload for that attempt is not in the repo, so I can't tell\n  whether it had the same shape. Check the first push of the new event\n  against the watch before trusting it.\n- The Intervals.icu documentation I could find did not specify the `hr` target\n  field names, so the `value`/`end` keys are kept from the original payload,\n  which the API accepted.\n- If bpm targets also come back wrong, the next thing to try is the\n  `start`/`end` range keys. The notes say `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` produced a\n  constant 101, so those names are wrong; `start`/`end` is untested.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":529,"cache_read_input_tokens":30992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":529},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2bea3dd-9e3e-4f96-bf4b-b795559c0a32","uuid":"ffb64173-0985-4c0a-ab90-505703a83b10","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:25:40.073Z","request_id":"req_011CgAoYNpm39WTJnCwcKWuK","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01ANP8KrcftzjhZBk1kQ5ovg":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/h-wAUkn2/ANSWER.md","content":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` sent every HR corridor as a percentage of LTHR:\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 88, \"end\": 93}\n```\n\nIntervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`), but\nwhen the workout reached the Forerunner 965 the target was resolved against the\nwatch's own zone bands, so each planned corridor displayed as a zone edge. The\nwatch's LTHR (168) differs from the athlete's (172), which is why the bands\nmoved but still never matched the planned range.\n\n## Change\n\n- **`gen.py`**: `hr_target()` now resolves the planned percentage to absolute\n  bpm using the plan's LTHR, and emits `\"units\": \"bpm\"`:\n  `value = round(lthr * lo / 100)`, `end = round(lthr * hi / 100)`.\n  `build_doc()` passes `plan[\"lthr\"]` down to each step. A plan without `lthr`\n  now fails with `KeyError` rather than silently using a default.\n- **`plans/tempo-run.json`**: added `\"lthr\": 172`.\n- **`README.md`**: corrected the note that said Intervals converts %LTHR to bpm\n  at export. The conversion now happens in `gen.py`.\n\n## Check\n\nRegenerated the event locally (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json`, not\npushed). The targets match the \"expected on watch\" column in\n`readback/watch-notes.md`:\n\n| step | planned | new target (bpm) | watch-notes expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 % | 117–129 | 117–129 |\n| Tempo | 88–93 % | 151–160 | 151–160 |\n| Float | 75–82 % | 129–141 | 129–141 |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 % | 112–124 | 112–124 |\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not push and have no live API or watch access here, so I have **not**\n  confirmed that Intervals exports `\"units\": \"bpm\"` targets to Garmin as custom\n  ranges. The watch-notes say an earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt displayed\n  214–249 bpm. The payload for that attempt is not in the repo, so I can't tell\n  whether it had the same shape. Check the first push of the new event\n  against the watch before trusting it.\n- The Intervals.icu documentation I could find did not specify the `hr` target\n  field names, so the `value`/`end` keys are kept from the original payload,\n  which the API accepted.\n- If bpm targets also come back wrong, the next thing to try is the\n  `start`/`end` range keys. The notes say `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` produced a\n  constant 101, so those names are wrong; `start`/`end` is untested.\n"}}}
