{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014yCf2aZpebuMfZME74mZzE","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/h-wAUkn2/ANSWER.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c2bea3dd-9e3e-4f96-bf4b-b795559c0a32","uuid":"21849f6f-62d8-49bd-8a37-46cbae78b9e9","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:25:43.900Z","tool_use_result":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-wAUkn2/ANSWER.md","oldString":"Intervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`), but\nwhen the workout reached the Forerunner 965 the target was resolved against the\nwatch's own zone bands, so each planned corridor displayed as a zone edge. The\nwatch's LTHR (168) differs from the athlete's (172), which is why the bands\nmoved but still never matched the planned range.","newString":"Intervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`). The\nwatch then showed each corridor as one of its own zone bands. The most likely\nexplanation is that the %LTHR target is handed to the watch as a zone-relative\ntarget, so it uses the watch's zones (LTHR 168) instead of the planned\ncorridor. This is inferred from the watch-notes, not confirmed against the\ndevice.","originalFile":"# HR ranges clamped to watch zones: fix\n\n## Cause\n\n`gen.py` sent every HR corridor as a percentage of LTHR:\n\n```json\n\"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 88, \"end\": 93}\n```\n\nIntervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`), but\nwhen the workout reached the Forerunner 965 the target was resolved against the\nwatch's own zone bands, so each planned corridor displayed as a zone edge. The\nwatch's LTHR (168) differs from the athlete's (172), which is why the bands\nmoved but still never matched the planned range.\n\n## Change\n\n- **`gen.py`**: `hr_target()` now resolves the planned percentage to absolute\n  bpm using the plan's LTHR, and emits `\"units\": \"bpm\"`:\n  `value = round(lthr * lo / 100)`, `end = round(lthr * hi / 100)`.\n  `build_doc()` passes `plan[\"lthr\"]` down to each step. A plan without `lthr`\n  now fails with `KeyError` rather than silently using a default.\n- **`plans/tempo-run.json`**: added `\"lthr\": 172`.\n- **`README.md`**: corrected the note that said Intervals converts %LTHR to bpm\n  at export. The conversion now happens in `gen.py`.\n\n## Check\n\nRegenerated the event locally (`python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json`, not\npushed). The targets match the \"expected on watch\" column in\n`readback/watch-notes.md`:\n\n| step | planned | new target (bpm) | watch-notes expected |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Warm-up easy | 68–75 % | 117–129 | 117–129 |\n| Tempo | 88–93 % | 151–160 | 151–160 |\n| Float | 75–82 % | 129–141 | 129–141 |\n| Cool-down | 65–72 % | 112–124 | 112–124 |\n\n## Not verified\n\n- I did not push and have no live API or watch access here, so I have **not**\n  confirmed that Intervals exports `\"units\": \"bpm\"` targets to Garmin as custom\n  ranges. The watch-notes say an earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt displayed\n  214–249 bpm. The payload for that attempt is not in the repo, so I can't tell\n  whether it had the same shape. Check the first push of the new event\n  against the watch before trusting it.\n- The Intervals.icu documentation I could find did not specify the `hr` target\n  field names, so the `value`/`end` keys are kept from the original payload,\n  which the API accepted.\n- If bpm targets also come back wrong, the next thing to try is the\n  `start`/`end` range keys. The notes say `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` produced a\n  constant 101, so those names are wrong; `start`/`end` is untested.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":8,"oldLines":11,"newStart":8,"newLines":12,"lines":[" \"hr\": {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": 88, \"end\": 93}"," ```"," ","-Intervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`), but","-when the workout reached the Forerunner 965 the target was resolved against the","-watch's own zone bands, so each planned corridor displayed as a zone edge. The","-watch's LTHR (168) differs from the athlete's (172), which is why the bands","-moved but still never matched the planned range.","+Intervals.icu stored that exactly (`readback/event-184233-as-sent.json`). The","+watch then showed each corridor as one of its own zone bands. The most likely","+explanation is that the %LTHR target is handed to the watch as a zone-relative","+target, so it uses the watch's zones (LTHR 168) instead of the planned","+corridor. This is inferred from the watch-notes, not confirmed against the","+device."," "," ## Change"," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014yCf2aZpebuMfZME74mZzE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAoZBRSf6gboJdBY9JQF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The generator now sends HR targets as absolute bpm instead of % of LTHR. I checked the output locally, but I have not confirmed it on the watch. I did not push anything.\n\n**What changed**\n- **`gen.py`**: `hr_target()` converts each planned percentage to bpm using the plan's LTHR, with `units: \"bpm\"`. `build_doc()` passes `plan[\"lthr\"]` through. A plan with no `lthr` now fails with a `KeyError`.\n- **`plans/tempo-run.json`**: added `\"lthr\": 172`.\n- **`README.md`**: the line saying Intervals converts %LTHR to bpm at export was wrong for this setup, so I corrected it.\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: explains the cause, the change, the check, and what is still unverified.\n\n**Check:** regenerating the tempo run gives Warm-up 117–129, Tempo 151–160, Float 129–141, Cool-down 112–124. Those match the \"expected on watch\" column in `readback/watch-notes.md`.\n\n**Not verified**\n- I could not confirm the cause against the device or the live API. My best explanation is that %LTHR targets are resolved against the watch's own zones (LTHR 168). The watch notes say an earlier `units: \"bpm\"` attempt showed 214–249 bpm, but that payload isn't in the repo, so I can't tell whether it had the same shape. Check the first push of this event against the watch before relying on it.\n- The web docs I found didn't specify the `hr` target field names. I kept `value`/`end` because the API accepted the original payload with them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":773,"cache_read_input_tokens":33936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":773},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management